## 1. Brand and open questions

The logo reads **"creperie hari's, waffle ice cream"**: a round badge, maroon and peach on a transparent background (an older version said "waffle pan cake"). The business is therefore a **creperie** (crepes, waffles, ice cream), a sweet place, and not a traditional restaurant.

**Not yet confirmed with the client. Do not hardcode these, keep them in one place (`data/site.ts`) so they are easy to change:**

- Public name: "Hari's" vs "Restoran Haris" (domain is `restoranharis.com`). Provisional: **Hari's** (`site.name`); in running text **Hari's Creperie** (`site.fullName`, used in the hero heading)
- Photos of the place and the food: **one so far**, `public/images/hero/mobile-bg.jpg` (the phone hero). The tablet and desktop hero images (`tablet.jpg`, `desktop.jpg`, see "Hero" in section 9) are still stock placeholders that must be replaced before launch.
- Address, phone, opening hours, social links, GPS coordinates: **unknown. Use clearly marked TODO placeholders, never invent them.**
- Menu categories: **Doručak, Ručak, Večera, Dezerti, Posni meni, Hari's Kolači, Sladoledi, Voćne torte, Piće** (given by the client on 2026-10-06, in this order; `data/menu.ts`). "Hari's" in "Hari's Kolači" is `site.name`, not typed. Dishes and prices: **unknown.** The example item data below is placeholder only.
- Original vector logo (SVG/AI/PDF): the provided file is `public/logoharis.png` (1200x1200 PNG, transparent background, the same badge as the printed menu). The older `public/logo.png` ("waffle pan cake", 567x529) is no longer used.

