## 2. Hard rules (never break these)

1. **`/meni` is the QR code target and must work forever.** Never rename, move or remove this route. Printed QR codes cannot be edited.
2. **Default language is Montenegrin (`me`) with NO URL prefix.** `restoranharis.com/meni` is always Montenegrin. Other languages use a prefix and a translated slug (see section 5).
3. **`localeDetection: false`** must stay in the routing config. Otherwise a tourist's browser language redirects the QR scan away from Montenegrin.
4. **No hardcoded text in components.** Website text goes in `messages/*.json`, dishes in `data/menu.ts`, contact info and brand name in `data/site.ts`. This includes `alt` text and `aria-label`s.
5. **All five `messages/*.json` files must have exactly the same keys.** Run `npm run i18n:check` before finishing any task.
6. Montenegrin is written in the **Latin script, ijekavian** ("preusmjerava", "mlijeko"). Customer-facing text uses formal **"Vi"**.
7. **Light theme only.** No dark mode, no theme toggle. Every page uses the cream background; the only non-cream surface is the maroon header bar (and its mobile panel).
8. **Do not invent business facts** (prices, address, hours, phone, dish names). Use `TODO` placeholders.
9. Keep pages as **server components**. Use `'use client'` only for interactive parts (language switcher, category nav).

