## 9. Design system

**Look:** warm, friendly, sweet. Round shapes echo the circular logo. Cream background on every page, maroon as the main color, peach for highlights. Restraint: one memorable element per screen, everything else quiet. The header (a maroon bar with the logo badge) is the site's one strong element; page sections stay on cream.

### Colors (sampled from the logo)

| Role | Hex | Use |
|---|---|---|
| Maroon | `#892E30` | Primary: buttons, prices, active states, links; header bar and mobile menu panel. The logo's exact maroon |
| Peach | `#FFD29F` | Secondary: chips, highlights, section backgrounds; header line and active header link |
| Cream | `#FFF2DC` | Page background (all pages), cards, popovers; text on maroon (header links, buttons). The logo's inner cream `#FFE4B8` mixed half with white |
| Cocoa | `#2E1517` | Body text |

Supporting shades, tuned to stay visible on the cream: `muted` `#F5E2C8` (soft panels), `accent` `#FFE4B8` (menu item hover, the logo's inner cream), `border`/`input` `#E6CBAD`, `secondary-foreground`/`accent-foreground` `#5A1A1E`, `muted-foreground` `#7A5A52`.

Contrast: cocoa on cream 15.4:1, maroon on cream 7.6:1, cream on maroon 7.6:1 (header links, buttons), maroon on peach 6.0:1, peach on maroon 6.0:1 (active header link), `muted-foreground` on cream 5.6:1 and on `muted` 4.9:1, `accent-foreground` on `accent` 10.6:1. **Never put peach text on a light background** (peach on cream is 1.3:1).

Tokens are defined in `app/globals.css` (shadcn variables overridden with the brand values, plus `bg-brand-maroon`, `bg-brand-peach`, `bg-brand-cream`, `bg-brand-cocoa` and the matching `text-`/`border-` classes). Use semantic classes (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`) first and brand classes only when needed. No white anywhere: cards and popovers (`--card`, `--popover`) are the same cream. They stand out from the page only through their shadow/ring or border, so keep those when restyling.

### Typography

- Headings: **Nunito**, rounded terminals like the logo (`font-heading`, applied to h1 to h4 globally; h1/h2 default to `font-extrabold`, the hero h1 uses `font-semibold`). All weights 200–1000 are available.
- Body: **Inter** (`font-sans`)
- Both must cover `latin`, `latin-ext`, `cyrillic` (č ć š ž đ, ğ ı ş, Russian)
- Line length under about 70 characters. Sentence case. No ALL CAPS eyebrow labels above headings.

**Fonts are self-hosted with `next/font/local`. Do not go back to `next/font/google`.** With Turbopack, Google Fonts sometimes returns `fonts.gstatic.com/l/font?kit=...&skey=...` URLs, which break the build with `Module not found: Can't resolve '@vercel/turbopack-next/internal/font/google/font'` / `next/font/google queries have exactly one entry`. The broken CSS is also saved in `.next/dev`, so the error survives restarts.

**`lib/fonts.ts`**
```ts
import localFont from "next/font/local"

export const nunito = localFont({
  src: "../app/fonts/Nunito.woff2",
  weight: "200 1000",
  variable: "--font-nunito",
  display: "swap",
})

export const inter = localFont({
  src: "../app/fonts/Inter.woff2",
  weight: "100 900",
  variable: "--font-inter",
  display: "swap",
})
```
The files in `app/fonts/` are variable woff2 fonts built from the originals in github.com/google/fonts (`ofl/nunito`, `ofl/inter`), cut down to the latin + latin-ext + cyrillic character ranges. Nunito keeps its full weight range 200–1000 (71 KB). Do not cut its weight range: the font has to be re-cut to do that, which makes the file bigger (600–900 was 82 KB). The first file had only 700–900, so `font-semibold` silently rendered as bold. Inter has all weights 100–900, with its optical-size axis fixed at 14 (142 KB). Their OFL licence files sit next to them. To add a weight or a font, build a new file the same way (the npm package `subset-font` works; this machine has no Python pip/venv).

In `app/[locale]/layout.tsx`: `<html lang={...} className={cn(nunito.variable, inter.variable, ...)}>`. The variable names must stay `--font-nunito` and `--font-inter`, because `globals.css` maps them to `--font-heading` and `--font-sans`. Do not rename them to `--font-sans`.

### Shape and layout

- Radius: large. Cards `rounded-2xl`/`rounded-3xl`, buttons and chips pill-shaped (`rounded-full`).
- Spacing: 8px grid, sections `py-16 md:py-24`, content `max-w-6xl`, menu page `max-w-2xl`.
- Mobile-first. Design at 375px width first, then scale up.
- Russian and Italian text is 20 to 30% longer than Montenegrin: no fixed-width buttons or headings.

### Components

Install with the CLI as needed: `button`, `tabs`, `card`, `badge`, `sheet` (mobile nav), `dropdown-menu`, `separator`, `skeleton`. Installed so far: `button`, `sheet`, `dropdown-menu`, `card`. The generated files import `cn` from the `cn` package (shadcn's clsx + tailwind-merge replacement, a dependency); that is correct.

The generated components contain some hardcoded English (for example the Sheet close button's `sr-only` "Close"). Do not ship that text: turn the built-in part off (`showCloseButton={false}`) and render your own with a translated label.

### Logo and images

- Header: the real logo (`public/logoharis.png`, static import) via `next/image`, with `site.name` as `alt`. Do not type the brand name as text instead of the logo.
- Favicon: square version of the logo as `app/icon.png`.
- OG image: `public/og.jpg`, 1200x630, logo on cream.
- Food photos: warm natural light, close-ups, one consistent aspect ratio, `rounded-2xl`, always `next/image`, compressed.

### Header (`components/layout/site-header.tsx`)

Based on the printed menu: a dark bar with the round logo badge hanging over a peach line. Built and checked at 375px, 640px and 1280px.

- Bar: `bg-brand-maroon`, height `h-(--header-bar)` (4rem, 5rem from `md`; the variable is in `globals.css` and the hero uses it too), 2px `border-brand-peach` at the bottom. Content `max-w-6xl`, `px-4`.
- Layering: the header is `relative z-40`, so the hanging logo is always above the page. Sections with layered backgrounds (like the hero) use `isolate` so their own z-indexes stay inside them. Popups and the sheet are z-50.
- Logo badge: `h-24` (`md:h-34`), absolutely positioned at the left and centred on the peach line (`top-[calc(100%+0px)] -translate-y-1/2`), so its lower half hangs into the page. That leaves 16px above it on phones and 12px from `md`. Pages start with `PageHeading` (below), which uses the strip beside the hanging half. Anything else that starts a page needs top padding of at least 48px (68px from `md`), which `py-16 md:py-24` gives. Do not go above about `h-32`/`md:h-40`, or the badge pokes out of the top of the bar.
- Tried and rejected by the client: pinning the logo 8px from the top (off-centre on the line), and a shorter bar (56/76px) to get both centring and a small top gap.
- Links: Meni · Galerija · O nama · Kontakt (`nav.*` messages; Galerija added 2026-10-06; at 640px, the tightest width, 101px stay free between the badge and the first link), Nunito bold, cream text. The current page is peach with `aria-current="page"` (`nav-links.tsx`, a client component because it reads the pathname). On a sub-page (Meni on `/meni/dorucak`) the link is peach too, with `aria-current="true"`.
- Right side: links (from `sm`), then the Facebook and Instagram logos and the language switcher, kept close together (`gap-1`). Below `sm`: logos, language switcher + hamburger, and the links open in a `Sheet` from the right (maroon panel, own translated close button, closes when a link is clicked).
- **Not sticky.** A sticky header would put the hanging badge over the menu page's sticky category chips.
- Focus on the bar: the default focus ring is maroon and invisible on the maroon bar, so header controls use a peach outline/ring (`header-styles.ts` for the icon buttons).
- The server component `site-header.tsx` renders three client parts: `nav-links.tsx`, `mobile-nav.tsx` and `language-switcher.tsx`.

### Page heading (`components/layout/page-heading.tsx`)

