### Motion and accessibility

**One motion style for the whole site**, defined at the top of `app/globals.css`. Use it everywhere and do not invent new timings:
- **Timing:** 200ms with `ease-brand` (`cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1)`, fast start, soft landing). It is set as Tailwind's default, so every `transition-colors`, `transition-opacity`, `transition` etc. gets it automatically. **Never add `duration-*` or `ease-*` classes.**
- **Popups that open and close** (dropdowns, popovers, selects, dialogs): add `transition-popup`, a fade plus a slight zoom (96% to 100%) from the trigger. It relies on Base UI's `data-starting-style`/`data-ending-style`. The dropdown menu uses it.
- **Sheets/drawers:** fade plus a short slide, with the same default timing (`components/ui/sheet.tsx`).
- **Content that appears** (loaded or swapped in): `animate-fade-in` (opacity only).
- **Hover/active states:** `transition-colors` (as on the header links).
- The generated shadcn components were changed to use this: the `tw-animate-css` classes (`animate-in`, `fade-in-0`, `zoom-in-95`, `duration-100`...) were removed from `dropdown-menu.tsx`, and the fixed durations/easing from `sheet.tsx`. Do the same to every new shadcn component you add.
- **Reduced motion:** `transition-popup` and the sheet fade only (no zoom/slide) when `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` is set. Keep that for anything new (`motion-reduce:transition-opacity`).
- Verified in Chrome: the dropdown fades in and out in about 200ms; the sheet and its overlay use 200ms + `ease-brand`; with reduced motion only opacity transitions.

Still little motion overall: no fade-and-slide on every section, no hover animation on every card. One deliberate moment at most.
- Visible keyboard focus (already set in `globals.css`), alt text on all images, `aria-label`s translated.

